abstract: >
  A two-part living document: a literature review challenging the "weakest link"
  framing and fact-based awareness training in cybersecurity (Part I), and an
  applied practitioner framework, the Human Firewall Framework (HFF), built on
  Cognitive Security, dual-process theory, persuasion science, memory
  neuroscience, inoculation theory, and behavior change science (Part II).
